{"family":"qb-a12-ma-s2","course":"ADV","year":12,"topic":"MA-S2","questions":[{"id":"A12-S2-013","group":"A12-S2-013","dp":"S2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Least-squares line through the means","prompt":"A least-squares regression line has gradient $3$. The means are $\\bar x=5$ and $\\bar y=20$. Find the equation of the line.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"3*x+5"},"hints":["The line passes through (x̄, ȳ).","Point-gradient form."],"ladder":{"nudge":"The line passes through (x̄, ȳ).","method":"Point-gradient form."},"steps":[{"h":"Through the means","d":"$y-20=3(x-5)$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"$y=3x+5$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = 3*x+20","why":"The intercept is not ȳ."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Uses (x̄, ȳ)","line":"y-20 = 3*(x-5)"},{"marks":1,"point":"y = 3x + 5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-014","group":"A12-S2-014","dp":"S2.2b","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"A residual","prompt":"The regression line is $y=2x+10$. Find the residual for the data point $(4,21)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3},"hints":["Find the predicted value.","Actual minus predicted.","Sign matters."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Find the predicted value.","method":"Actual minus predicted.","worked":"Sign matters."},"steps":[{"h":"Predicted","d":"$2(4)+10=18$; residual $21-18=3$"}],"traps":[{"value":-3,"why":"Residual is actual minus predicted."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-022","group":"A12-S2-022","dp":"S2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"A tidy standard deviation","prompt":"Find the population standard deviation of $2,4,4,4,5,5,7,9$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2},"hints":["Find the mean.","Average the squared deviations.","Square root."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Find the mean.","method":"Average the squared deviations.","worked":"Square root."},"steps":[{"h":"Mean","d":"$5$"},{"h":"Variance","d":"$\\tfrac{9+1+1+1+0+0+4+16}{8}=4$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"That is the variance."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Variance 4","line":"32/8"},{"marks":1,"point":"2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-029","group":"A12-S2-029","dp":"S2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Mean of two combined groups","prompt":"A group of $10$ students has mean mark $70$ and another group of $15$ has mean $80$. Find the mean of all $25$ students.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":76},"hints":["Find each total.","Divide by 25."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Find each total.","method":"Divide by 25."},"steps":[{"h":"Totals","d":"$700+1200=1900$"},{"h":"Mean","d":"$\\tfrac{1900}{25}$"}],"traps":[{"value":75,"why":"Averaged the two means without weights."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Total 1900","line":"1900/25"},{"marks":1,"point":"76","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-041","group":"A12-S2-041","dp":"S2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Standard deviation of a small set","prompt":"Find the population standard deviation of $2,4,4,4,5,5,7,9$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2},"hints":["Mean 5.","Square the deviations.","Average then root."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Mean 5.","method":"Square the deviations.","worked":"Average then root."},"steps":[{"h":"Mean","d":"$5$"},{"h":"Variance","d":"$\\tfrac{9+1+1+1+0+0+4+16}{8}=4$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"That is the variance."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-047","group":"A12-S2-047","dp":"S2.2b","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Residual sign","prompt":"The regression line is $\\hat y=12+3x$. A data point is $(4,20)$. Find the residual.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-4},"hints":["Predict at x = 4.","Actual − predicted."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Predict at x = 4.","method":"Actual − predicted."},"steps":[{"h":"Residual","d":"$20-24$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"Actual minus predicted."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-048","group":"A12-S2-048","dp":"S2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Effect of removing an outlier on the mean","prompt":"Five values have mean $12$. One value, $28$, is removed. Find the new mean.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":8},"hints":["Total 60.","Divide by 4."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total 60.","method":"Divide by 4."},"steps":[{"h":"Sum","d":"$60-28=32$, over $4$"}],"traps":[{"value":12,"why":"Removing a large value lowers the mean."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"8","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-054","group":"A12-S2-054","dp":"S2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Coefficient of determination meaning","prompt":"A regression has $r=0.8$. What percentage of the variation in $y$ is explained by $x$?","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":64},"hints":["r² is explained variation.","As a percentage."],"ladder":{"nudge":"r² is explained variation.","method":"As a percentage."},"steps":[{"h":"Square","d":"$0.8^{2}$"}],"traps":[{"value":80,"why":"Square r."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"64%","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-058","group":"A12-S2-058","dp":"S2.1b","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Cumulative frequency from a table","prompt":"Scores $1,2,3,4$ have frequencies $3,7,6,4$. Find the median.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2.5},"hints":["Total 20.","Cumulative 3, 10, 16, 20.","Average the 10th and 11th."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total 20.","method":"Cumulative 3, 10, 16, 20.","worked":"Average the 10th and 11th."},"steps":[{"h":"Position","d":"$10$th and $11$th values are $2$ and $3$"}],"traps":[{"value":2,"why":"The 11th value is 3."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"2.5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-061","group":"A12-S2-061","dp":"S2.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Standard deviation change after adding a constant","prompt":"Every score in a set with SD $6.5$ is increased by $10$. State the new SD.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":6.5},"hints":["Shifting moves the centre.","Spread is unchanged.","Same SD."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Shifting moves the centre.","method":"Spread is unchanged.","worked":"Same SD."},"steps":[{"h":"Shift","d":"Spread unchanged"}],"traps":[{"value":16.5,"why":"Adding a constant does not change spread."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"6.5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-084","group":"A12-S2-084","dp":"S2.1b","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Ogive percentile for a cut-off","prompt":"Using the ogive in a set of $200$ scores (points $(20,0)$, $(40,30)$, $(60,110)$, $(80,180)$, $(100,200)$), estimate the score at the $90$th percentile by linear interpolation.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":80},"hints":["90% of 200.","Locate on the graph."],"ladder":{"nudge":"90% of 200.","method":"Locate on the graph."},"steps":[{"h":"Target","d":"$180$th score"},{"h":"Read","d":"Exactly at $(80,180)$"}],"traps":[{"value":90,"why":"90% of 200 is 180."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"180th position","line":"180"},{"marks":1,"point":"80","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-105","group":"A12-S2-105","dp":"S2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Combined mean of two groups","prompt":"Class A ($20$ students) has mean $65$ and class B ($30$ students) has mean $70$. Find the combined mean.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":68},"hints":["Total marks per class.","Divide by 50."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total marks per class.","method":"Divide by 50."},"steps":[{"h":"Totals","d":"$1300+2100$"},{"h":"Divide","d":"$\\tfrac{3400}{50}$"}],"traps":[{"value":67.5,"why":"Weight by class size."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Totals","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"68","answer":true}]},{"id":"A12-S2-111","group":"A12-S2-111","dp":"S2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Effect of adding a value on the mean","prompt":"The mean of $9$ numbers is $12$. A tenth number is added and the mean becomes $13$. Find the tenth number.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":22},"hints":["Total = mean × count.","New total."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Total = mean × count.","method":"New total."},"steps":[{"h":"Totals","d":"$1